D09|Dialogs reached from other dialogs|Offer of peace (after a battle)|After the "Battle ended" box, a window "Offer of peace" with Yes and No: the opponent is willing to end the war on the terms printed. The terms that can actually be offered here are the honourable peace (no reparations or penalties); No continues the war.|a tactical battle in which a human took part and the winner has fewer armies than the loser, the loser's unity is above 500 and it has more than 7 cities, and a 2-in-5 roll passes; the form also holds reparation and end-trade/alliance text branches, which the code's gate makes unreachable here|coverage.md §1 'Accept a post-battle peace (TBattlePols)' (driven, lab2_a_after_no.SAV); F:2026-10-04-battle-probe.md ('Offer of peace' in 3 of 17 battles; lab2_a_after_no.SAV, lab2_b_post.SAV); form TBattlePols; X:TBattlePols_InitializeForm 0x004577ec; R:decompiled-war-cascade-and-peace-paths.md §2.3 and the path table; docs/rules-digest.md §6 (Post-battle peace)|[confirmed]|needed
