E01|Turn-start and turn-end events|Diplomatic offer box at turn start|At the start of a human seat's turn an OK-only box "X wants to trade with Y." or "X wants to form an alliance with Y." may appear. It never changes a relation (the player makes the trade or alliance on the relations screen) and lapses at the next turn start; loading a save shows a pending one again, unless it was accepted before saving.|one nation is drawn at random and offers only if it is at peace (relation 0) with the human, alive, computer-controlled and a 1-in-3 roll passes [report]; a trade offer also needs the proposer's tax base above the human's poorest partner's (or 0 with fewer than 3 partners) and a poorer partner of its own; an alliance offer needs the proposer in the human's neighbour mask and the human at war with nobody [report]|coverage.md §3 'Turn start (AI offers)' (BASE.SAV turn 0720, Bithynia; test end-turn 0721, Celtiberia); X:TPremierForm_StartTurn 0x0045ac5c; R:news-log-format-and-messages.md Q5, decompiled-ai-offers-to-human-seats.md|[confirmed]|useful
E02|Turn-start and turn-end events|Round tick (week, season, year)|After the 16th seat the round tick runs once: the calendar advances two weeks (weeks 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11), and when the week wraps to 1 the season advances (and the year, 270 BC down to 250 BC, after winter); two news lines are added (a blank and "Week  N      Season      YYYBC"; seen in T_ATTACK.SAV). [report] The quarterly tick and the mercenary restock run when the week wraps to 1, before the season advances, and the tick applies the season before the advance.|all 16 seats have played|tests/results.md 'attack' (news tail "Week  3      Spring      270BC" after the first End turn, T_ATTACK.SAV); R:decompiled-turn-and-calendar-sequencing.md; news-log-format-and-messages.md Q3 (338 of 342 headers preceded by a blank); H:'Time'|[confirmed]|needed
E03|Turn-start and turn-end events|Quarterly tick|Once a quarter (at the end of the week-11 turn, before the season advances) the order is: upkeep (ships, regular units to the treasury, mercenaries to their army's purse, the 40 recruitment slots), wealth and tax base rebuilt, the city loop (growth, loyalty, rebellion), the nation loop (mobilisation -3, income, trade, unity, AI debt test), relation thaw. The treasury changes by taxBase x rate div 100 + taxBase div 4, minus 3 x ships (launched fleets only), minus unit and slot upkeep, minus cities x 7 and wealth div 20,000, plus partner taxBase div 12 per trade or alliance partner. Units, slots and ships are billed with no balance check: the treasury can go negative and regular units never desert.|the round tick in which the week wraps to 1|R:decompiled-quarterly-billing-and-economy.md, upkeep-payment-and-desertion.md, decompiled-quarterly-rebellion.md; X:FUN_00451b40; coverage.md §4 'Quarterly billing and taxes' (not yet seen)|[derived]|needed
E04|Turn-start and turn-end events|Supply use and morale|An army on the map uses ((90 - v) x troops) div 20,000 supplies a turn, v = 50 spring, 80 summer and autumn, 20 winter (troops/500 in spring, troops/2000 in summer and autumn, 7 x troops/2000 in winter); an army aboard a fleet uses a flat troops div 200 all year; a fleet loses one ton per ship a turn. Supply below 10 percent after the use costs morale and a move (see E29); mercenaries refuse to join an army under 15 percent supply.|every round tick|H:'Time', 'Armies'; R:rules-digest.md §2 (supply-driven-morale-and-fleet-attrition.md); coverage.md §4 'Supply consumption and seasonal rates' (not yet seen)|[derived]|needed
E05|Turn-start and turn-end events|Fleet completion|A fleet ordered through Build fleet stays at (0,0) while its countdown (24, minus 2 a tick) runs, so it appears at its city after 12 turns; [code] on launch it has condition 100, supplies 50 and money 0, and costs nothing until launched (its news line is code-only, row L07b).|a fleet under construction; the order needs a free coastal city|coverage.md §4 'Fleets: build, launch' (saves/fleet-port-antium-0734.SAV: launched at 0732); X:FUN_0044a050; the news line itself is code-only (news-log-format-and-messages.md Q4 #3)|[confirmed]|needed
E06|Turn-start and turn-end events|Storms at sea|Every turn each launched fleet is rolled for a storm: damage = max(1, Random(100 - condition)/10), doubled (at most 5) in winter, tripled (at most 8) on rough sea; away from one of its own cities it becomes 2 x damage + 1 (with a 1-in-20 spike to 30 in winter), next to one it is halved. Damage under 6 only lowers condition; 6 or more also removes ships and condition and costs an army aboard casualties (whole units lost when d exceeds 70). A fleet whose condition falls below 40 is lost with its army ("A fleet belonging to N is lost at sea."); one that is out of supply also loses 3 moves and up to 1 condition a turn. Damage is announced as "damaged in a storm".|a launched fleet, every round tick|F:2026-10-03-storms-and-losses-at-sea.md (NAT_seed1_13_0727_seat02.SAV: 'A fleet belonging to Ptolemaic is lost at sea.'); X:FUN_004514ec; H:'Fleets'|[confirmed]|useful
E07|Turn-start and turn-end events|Weather (rough sea)|Twenty fixed sea-region centres are rolled each tick: spring 1/15 (radius 4) in weeks before 6, else 1/30 (3); summer 1/40 (2); autumn 1/30 (3) in weeks before 7, else 1/15 (4); winter 1/5 (5). A hit paints calm sea as rough sea for a week; rough sea costs a fleet 3 moves a tile and raises storm damage. [report] Weather affects fleets only.|every round tick|R:decompiled-weather-events.md, decompiled-map-code1-overlay.md; X:FUN_00451304; the fleet panel shows Sea calm or rough (X:TInformation_ShowFleetDetails)|[derived]|cosmetic
E08|Turn-start and turn-end events|AI wars, alliances and peace|The player sees the AI's wars, alliances and peace treaties only as news lines (rows L03, L03b, L06); the conditions under which the AI declares war are in row E22.|AI seats|SS:FI_b1_01_main.png (the treaty lines written after the Week 1 header); R:news-log-format-and-messages.md Q4 #1, #2, #14-#18; decompiled-war-cascade-and-peace-paths.md|[derived]|useful
E09|Turn-start and turn-end events|Siege attempts|A failed siege (strength not above defence; ties go to the defender) costs every besieging unit troops/(Random(15)+105) x r, r = max(1, min(15, def x 6 div atk)) (units left under a tenth of their size, a fifth for mercenaries, are deleted), erodes the city's loyalty, fortification and population, sets the army's moves to 0, and writes "N fails to capture C   (A)."|an army next to an enemy city|C:§1 'Attack a city (siege)' (T_ATTACK.SAV: army 23,700 -> 21,765, Felsina loyalty 79 -> 76, fort 68 -> 65, pop 26 -> 25, news "Rome fails to capture Felsina (Gaul)."); saves/siege-felsina-failed-0721.SAV; R:decompiled-defection-and-siege-attrition.md|[confirmed]|needed
E11|Turn-start and turn-end events|City capture, defection and elimination|A successful siege (strength above defence) transfers the city ("C   (A)  falls to B."). A capture that leaves the loser with fewer than 6 cities (or takes a capital that cannot be moved) conquers the whole nation at once ("A conquers B."); cities also defect (rows E13, E14).|a siege that succeeds|R:decompiled-city-capture-resolution.md, decompiled-defection-and-siege-attrition.md, decompiled-elimination-cleanup.md, news-log-format-and-messages.md Q4 #5, #9, #11 (40, 18 and 2 events in the research saves); X:FUN_0044b27c, FUN_0044bed8, FUN_0044c528; coverage.md §4 'City capture', 'Defection cascade', 'Conquest' (not yet seen in this repository)|[derived]|needed
E12|Turn-start and turn-end events|Automatic resupply on a move|When a human army's move ends against a non-hostile city, the army is filled to troops div 100 from that city's stock without the Supply dialog. At an own city the fill is free; a purse over 1,000 sends the excess to the treasury, and a purse under 500 receives 500 from the treasury only if the treasury is above 0. At a foreign city at most money div 5 tons, costing tons div 5. The AI does it every turn for each non-hostile city within 4 tiles.|a move that ends next to a friendly or neutral city (a hostile city is a siege instead)|X:FUN_0044f6d8; R:supply-capacity-rounding.md, upkeep-payment-and-desertion.md; docs/rules-digest.md §2 "How an army resupplies" 2; docs/rules-digest.md §5 "Adjacency and attack orders"; coverage.md §4 'Auto-resupply next to an own city' (not yet seen on a controlled save)|[derived]|needed
E13|Turn-start and turn-end events|Rebellion and rebirth|Each quarter a non-capital city with loyalty below 30 rebels. If its owner is not its allegiance nation, it returns to the allegiance nation when that nation is alive, and when that nation is dead the city triggers the nation's rebirth (which needs more than 7 disloyal cities). If its owner is its allegiance nation, it goes to a nation at war with the owner that has an army within 9 tiles, else to the best-placed live neighbour.|a quarterly tick; a non-capital city with loyalty below 30|X:FUN_0044c204, FUN_00451b40; R:decompiled-quarterly-rebellion.md; docs/rules-digest.md §5 "Capture, defection cascade, conquest, rebellion"; coverage.md §4 'Rebellion, rebirth' (never observed; no save held a city below loyalty 39)|[derived]|useful
E14|Turn-start and turn-end events|Capture effects and defection cascade|A capture flips the owner and keeps the allegiance; the winner's unity rises by 9 (to at most 990) and the loser's falls by 15; wealth (pop x 3000) and tax base move to the winner, the old owner's queued units at the city are cleared, and loyalty becomes min(90, 140 - L) when the capturer is the city's allegiance nation, else between 40 and 60. After each capture every other city of the loser defects to the capturer, with no battle, when all hold: it is no nation's capital and lies less than 10 tiles from the attacking army; the loser's unity after its -15 is below 650 and the city's loyalty is below 65; its defence (divided by 3 if its allegiance is the capturer) is below the attacker's strength. A defected city keeps its population and fortification; the receiver's unity rises by 3, the loser's falls by 20 (not below 250), and loyalty becomes between 50 and 65.|a successful siege|X:FUN_0044bb18, FUN_0044ba1c; R:decompiled-city-capture-resolution.md, decompiled-defection-and-siege-attrition.md; docs/rules-digest.md §5 "Capture, defection cascade, conquest, rebellion"; coverage.md §4 'City capture', 'Defection cascade' (not yet seen)|[derived]|needed
E15|Turn-start and turn-end events|Mercenary pay and desertion|Each quarter a mercenary unit is paid ((troops div 200) x price x quality) div 5 from its own army's purse, never from the treasury. Units are taken in slot order; if the purse is 0 or less when a mercenary slot comes up, the whole unit leaves with troops div 100 tons of supplies (the army's last unit takes its place), with no news line and no morale change; the purse is then floored at 0. The tick never refills a purse (only the dialogs and the automatic top-up at an own city do).|a quarterly tick; mercenary units in an army|R:upkeep-payment-and-desertion.md; decompiled-fleet-tax-and-mercenary-formulas.md; docs/rules-digest.md §3 "Mercenary pay and desertion"; X:FUN_00451b40; coverage.md §4 'Mercenary hire, pay, desertion' (hire only seen)|[derived]|needed
E16|Turn-start and turn-end events|Debt and deposition of an AI leader|An AI nation that fails the debt test (treasury below -(wealth div 500) or below -20,000, or unity below 400) has a 1-in-9 chance each quarter of deposing its leader, which resets a negative treasury to 0 and writes "N depose their leader L."; a human in that state is tested at the start of each of his turns and the game ends instead (row V04).|a quarterly tick; an AI nation that fails the test|X:FUN_0044c8f0, FUN_00451b40; R:upkeep-payment-and-desertion.md; docs/rules-digest.md §3 "Debt and deposition"; news-log-format-and-messages.md Q4 #13 (2 events)|[derived]|useful
E17|Turn-start and turn-end events|Tax effects|Each quarter, per city: loyalty rises by Random(4) if the tax rate is under 11 and loyalty is under 80; with a 1-in-3 chance loyalty falls by Random(tax rate) div 8; population grows by d = (maxPop - pop) >> 2 reduced by d x tax/120 and by mobilisation, skipped when a hostile army is adjacent. Per nation: unity = min(990, max(300, unity + 25 - tax/2 - mobilisation/5)) and mobilisation falls by 3 (not below 0).|a quarterly tick|R:city-population-growth.md, decompiled-quarterly-billing-and-economy.md; docs/rules-digest.md §3 "Tax effects"; H:'Taxation'; X:FUN_00451b40|[derived]|needed
E18|Turn-start and turn-end events|Mobilisation rate|Placing a recruit order raises mobilisation to min(100, rate + 1 + troops x 1000 div wealth) and is refused at 100; disbanding a queued order lowers it by 1 + troops x 1000 / wealth; it falls by 3 each quarter (not below 0). Mobilizing a unit does not change it. A high rate cuts city supply production (x (1 - mob/200)), population growth and unity.|Recruit unit orders; a quarterly tick|R:decompiled-mobilization-and-mercenary-restock.md, decompiled-recruitment-cost-formula.md; docs/rules-digest.md §4 "Placing an order", "Mobilizing"; saves/recruit-hi3200-0720.SAV is the measured order (30 -> 32) in C:§1 'Recruit a unit'; X:TArmyRecruits_RecruitUnit|[derived]|needed
E19|Turn-start and turn-end events|City supply stock and winter famine|Every round each city adds s = pop x (v - 40)/10 to its stock (v as in E04: pop in spring, 4 x pop in summer and autumn, minus 2 x pop in winter), reduced by s x mobilisation/200; with an at-war army adjacent (3 x 3) the change is at most 0; the stock stays between 0 and 10 x pop; with an empty stock in winter a city loses 1 loyalty with a 1-in-3 chance.|every round tick|R:city-population-growth.md, decompiled-turn-and-calendar-sequencing.md (correction note); docs/rules-digest.md §2 "City supply stock"; X:FUN_004514ec; coverage.md §4 'Winter attrition of city stocks' (not yet seen)|[derived]|useful
E20|Turn-start and turn-end events|Army moves per turn and walking|An army's moves each turn are 10 - min(5, troops div 20,000), minus 1 under 10 percent supply, recomputed only at the tick; join, a field battle (attacker), a siege attempt, embark or disembark, and creation (for a human) set moves to 0, and an army needs moves above 0 to be selected. One click walks a straight line paying each tile (calm sea 1, rough sea 3 for fleets; plain and desert 1; forest 2; mountains and rivers 4); a human's walk stops at the first unaffordable step and keeps the remaining moves (the AI loses them all).|every round tick; a move click|R:army-moves-field-signed-and-the-ffff-underflow.md, decompiled-army-movement-and-river-cost.md, terrain-move-cost-table-in-dat.md; docs/rules-digest.md §5 "Moves", "Walking"; C:§1 'Move army' (river tile costs 4: T_MOVE.SAV)|[derived]|needed
E21|Turn-start and turn-end events|Siege resolution and attrition|A siege compares atk = (troops, archers counted triple) div 80 x morale with def = loyalty x 150 + fortification x 250 + population (thousands) x 200, times 5/3 if the city is a capital and its loyalty is above 59, times 4/5 if its owner is not its allegiance nation, plus half the owner's queued troops there, times 9/10 if the attacker is the allegiance nation; a pending fortification order is first cut to its built part. Loyalty, fortification and population erode win or lose (never below 3/4), population not below maxPop/6 + 1; atk above def takes the city, ties go to the defender; the besieger's moves become 0.|a siege click on an enemy city|X:FUN_0044b27c; R:decompiled-city-capture-resolution.md, decompiled-defection-and-siege-attrition.md; docs/rules-digest.md §5 "Siege"; C:§1 'Attack a city (siege)' (T_ATTACK.SAV: a failed siege measured)|[derived]|needed
E22|Turn-start and turn-end events|AI diplomacy toward the player and cooldowns|An AI nation declares war on a human only when it is at war with nobody, its mobilisation is 40 or less and it is not winter; the target borders it (neighbour mask) and is not protected by an ally; and 8 x P(me)/P(target) is above 10 (P = wealth/20,000 x unity/100); it then declares with a 1-in-10 chance per turn. Leaving trade writes a cooldown of -8, an alliance -24, ending a war -18; each quarter every negative value gains 1 and with a 1-in-3 chance becomes min(0, v + 3), but only for nations indexed 0 to 7 (a code bug).|AI turns; quarterly tick|R:decompiled-ai-offers-to-human-seats.md, decompiled-diplomacy-peace-terms-and-instant-battles.md, decompiled-war-cascade-and-peace-paths.md; docs/rules-digest.md §7; coverage.md §4 'AI declares war on Rome' (not yet seen)|[derived]|useful
E23|Turn-start and turn-end events|Recruitment queue as garrison and training|The recruitment queue of up to 40 units is the city garrison (shown beside a city's fortification). A slot starts at state 0 and gains 2 each round up to 24; a mobilized unit's quality is state/4, fixed; the player may mobilize at state above 15 (quality 4 or more), the AI waits for 24. Queued units cost upkeep even when not ready, add half their troops to the city's siege defence and are cleared when the city is captured.|every round tick|R:ptolemy-run-readiness-ladder-and-mobilization-rate-confirmed.md, decompiled-mobilization-and-mercenary-restock.md; docs/rules-digest.md §4 "The recruitment queue", "Readiness and quality"; H:'Recruit unit' (16 weeks to train, 24 to full effectiveness); coverage.md §4 'Recruitment readiness and mobilization' (saves/mobilize-new-army-0720.SAV)|[derived]|needed
E24|Turn-start and turn-end events|Fleet supply, condition and moves|A fleet holds 8 tons per ship and uses one ton per ship a turn; a carried army uses troops div 200. Its moves are 30 - (ships - 50)/10, minus troops aboard/100/ships + 1 when carrying, minus 3 with 0 supplies, and (70 - condition) >> 2 when condition is below 70.|every round tick|R:supply-driven-morale-and-fleet-attrition.md, field-recruitment-uniform-attrition-and-fleet-drift.md; docs/rules-digest.md §8; H:'Fleets'; F:2026-10-02-fleets-sail-and-drift.md|[derived]|useful
E25|Turn-start and turn-end events|New game start state|A new game shuffles the 16-seat turn order and copies each nation's start (relations, queue, armies, mercenary pool) from the DAT; the AI seats before the first human seat have already moved, so the start differs with the chosen nation: five nations start with no army (Numidia, Greece, Illyria, Dacia, Armenia) and only Carthage and Ptolemaic have a fleet.|File > New|F:2026-10-02-start-as-each-nation.md (turn order and start per nation); R:decompiled-new-game-mercenary-fill.md, 2026-09-29-new-game-recruitment-queues-come-from-the-dat.md; docs/rules-digest.md §1 "Calendar and turn sequencing", §10; C:§1 'New game (any nation human; several for several human seats)' (NEW_a.SAV = NEW_b.SAV = BASE.SAV)|[derived]|needed
E26|Turn-start and turn-end events|AI mercenary hiring|The AI hires every live mercenary offer on any city within 4 tiles of an army; the hire is free and has no troop, supply or fleet cap. Offers are restocked each quarter (row E10).|the AI nation is at war with someone and the army's purse is above 50|R:decompiled-mercenary-offer-list-and-position.md, decompiled-mobilization-and-mercenary-restock.md; docs/rules-digest.md §4 "Mercenaries"|[derived]|cosmetic
E27|Turn-start and turn-end events|Trade and tribute income|Per quarter the treasury gains taxBase x tax rate div 100 + taxBase div 4 (taxes and tribute) and, for each trade or alliance partner (relation 1 or 2), the partner's taxBase div 12; the Balance sheet shows taxes, tribute and trade.|a quarterly tick; trade or alliance partners|R:nation-tax-base-and-city-economy-fields.md, decompiled-quarterly-billing-and-economy.md; H:'Nations' (trade income); SS:FI_b1_16_balance_sheet.png (trade 29 for Rome); coverage.md §4 'Trade income' (trade made: saves/trade-numidia-0720.SAV)|[derived]|needed
E28|Turn-start and turn-end events|Elimination cleanup|A capture that leaves the loser with fewer than 6 cities (or takes a capital that cannot be moved) annexes every remaining city at once; the loser's armies and its fleets at sea are deleted with their money and supplies, fleets under construction go to the conqueror and the neighbour masks merge. An eliminated nation shows unity 0 and capital 0xFFFF, and an eliminated human gets the End of Game screen and the seat turns AI.|a capture that leaves fewer than 6 cities|X:FUN_0044c528; R:decompiled-elimination-cleanup.md, galatia-elimination-and-city-resupply-confirmed.md; docs/rules-digest.md §9; SS:FI_b1_20_nation_carthage.png (status panel layout)|[derived]|needed
E29|Turn-start and turn-end events|Army morale from supply|After the supply use of each round: supply below 10 percent costs 2 morale (not below 51) and 1 move; 10 to 15 percent changes nothing; above 15 percent adds 1 morale (not above 70). A new army starts at morale 59; at 0 percent it loses 2 a tick. Morale multiplies siege and field strength and seeds each unit's battle morale; supply is the only path from supply to morale and starvation never kills troops.|every round tick|R:supply-driven-morale-and-fleet-attrition.md, decompiled-unit-map-orders-and-record-fields.md Part 1; docs/rules-digest.md §2 "Supply drives morale and moves"; H:'Armies'; coverage.md §4 'Morale from supply' (not yet seen)|[derived]|useful
E10|Turn-start and turn-end events|Mercenary offers appear and are taken|Fifty fixed mercenary slots sit on city tiles; each quarter an empty slot refills with probability 85 percent and a live offer is replaced with probability 1/9 (quality 5 to 9); a hired offer leaves the pool (saves/merc-hire-free-0720.SAV). The Show mercenaries views and the right-click list show the offers.|every quarterly tick|SS:FI_b1_22_show_all_mercenaries.png; R:decompiled-mobilization-and-mercenary-restock.md, decompiled-new-game-mercenary-fill.md; C:§1 'Hire mercenaries'|[confirmed]|useful
L01|News and messages|News log lines|[report] forty slots of at most 60 characters; the log shows the oldest line at the top; the display shows them in the Information window.|none|R:news-log-format-and-messages.md Q1; SS:FI_b1_01_main.png|[confirmed]|needed
